[IMP] account,*: unify partner identifiers behind a single JSON field

Before this change each localization maintained its own partner
identifier field (FR SIREN/SIRET, DK CVR, SG UEN, NO EN, IT Codice
Fiscale, etc.) with fragmented validation, views, etc.
Every new country meant another column, another constraint, another view,
another place to forget.

These identifiers are all instances of the same concept:
an administrative identifier, distinct from the tax ID (VAT) so we think
they belong in a single structure.
This commit adds `additional_identifiers` a JSON field on `res.partner`
keyed by identifier type (e.g. `FR_SIREN`, `DK_CVR`, `EAN_GLN`), backed by
centralized metadata/validation.

Some advantages of the solution:
* Validate and normalize identifiers in one place, regardless of
  localization package installed.
* Deduce related identifiers automatically (BE VAT => BE BCE/KBO, FR SIRET => FR SIREN, …).
* Centralize all identifiers in one place in the view, instead of having them
  split all over the place.
* Add identifier in stable without the need of a new module.
* Still keep flexibility with "proxy fields" (compute/inverse targetting
  one item in the JSON).

This commit is only the first step of a bigger refactor.
Still need to be done:
* Peppol refactor - replace eas/endpoint to avoid redundancy, while still
  allowing corner-case configuration.
* UBL/CII refactor - use the new JSON values instead of the company registry.
* Totally deprecate the company registry field that is a big "fourre-tout".

